  {
    "id": "86d4c0nx3",
    "name": "Learning on Wed 23-Sep-2026",
    "description": "Revised Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) by incorporating advanced retrieval techniques beyond simple keyword matching. Instead of relying solely on dense embeddings, it leverages traditional ranking methods like BM25 and hybrid approaches that combine lexical and semantic signals. The goal is to improve precision and recall in retrieving contextually relevant documents for downstream tasks. Alongside implementation, the process involves reviewing and synthesizing research papers on retrieval algorithms, hybrid search strategies, and evaluation benchmarks to ensure the design is grounded in state-of-the-art methods. This dual focus—practical experimentation with retrieval models and theoretical study of academic work—creates a robust foundation for building more reliable and explainable RAG systems.",
    "status": "to do",
    "priority": "normal",
